CRASH-12: index the Link array with the link, not its upstream node, in findSFLinkQual()

findSFLinkQual() sets j = Link[i].node1 (a node index) for the upstream
node's quality, and the API mass-flux block added for 5.3.0 then used j as a
link index: Link[j].apiExtQualMassFlux[p] and Link[j].totalLoad[p]. Under
STEADY routing with any pollutant this reads past the Link array whenever an
upstream node index is >= the number of links, and otherwise applies another
link's flux. Use Link[i], the conduit being processed, as findLinkQual() does.

Requires: NUM-01

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-12_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
index 3e47df1..a1a8ad8 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/qualrout.c
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@ void findSFLinkQual(int i, double qSeep, double fEvap, double tStep)
         qIn = fabs(Conduit[k].q1) * barrels;
         v1 = Link[i].oldVolume;
 
-        cOut = Link[j].apiExtQualMassFlux[p];
+        cOut = Link[i].apiExtQualMassFlux[p];
 
         // --- a link with no water (v1 + qIn*tStep = 0) takes no flux
         //     (the division below would give 0/0 = NaN)
@@ -461,7 +461,7 @@ void findSFLinkQual(int i, double qSeep, double fEvap, double tStep)
             c2 -= cOut;
             
             cOut = cOut * (v1 + qIn * tStep) ;
-            Link[j].totalLoad[p] -= cOut;
+            Link[i].totalLoad[p] -= cOut;
 
             cOut = cOut/ tStep;
             massbal_addOutflowQual(p, cOut, FALSE);
@@ -472,7 +472,7 @@ void findSFLinkQual(int i, double qSeep, double fEvap, double tStep)
             c2 += cOut;
 
             cOut = cOut * (v1 + qIn * tStep);
-            Link[j].totalLoad[p] += cOut;
+            Link[i].totalLoad[p] += cOut;
 
             cOut = cOut/ tStep;
             massbal_addInflowQual(EXTERNAL_INFLOW, p, cOut);
